  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\int_0^\\pi x f(\\sin x) d x=A \\int_0^{\\pi / 2} f(\\sin x) d x$, then $A$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\pi$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_0^\\pi x f(\\sin x) d x=\\int_0^\\pi(\\pi-x) f(\\sin x) d x=\\pi \\int_0^\\pi f(\\sin x) d x-I \\quad(\\sin c e f(2 a-x)=f(x))$\n$\\Rightarrow I=\\pi \\int_0^{\\pi / 2} f(\\sin x) d x \\Rightarrow A=\\pi$"
  }
}